# The aLLManac — the STABLE channel.  Image pins, nothing else.
# =============================================================================
# A channel is one file of image pins.  `.env` picks it with ALMANAC_CHANNEL
# and `just` hands it to compose ahead of `.env`, so a box's own `.env` can
# still override any single pin.  Two channels ship:
#
#   stable  — what a course runs on.  Every pin here was deployed, walked as
#             a student and a professor, and committed.  Bump deliberately:
#             edit, deploy to latest first, verify, then move it here.
#   latest  — the dev playground.  Release candidates and moving tags, so an
#             upgrade is validated on a box nobody teaches on before stable
#             moves.  Expect it to break; that is what it is for.
#
# Every deployment reads exactly one channel.  A box does not mix them.
# =============================================================================

# LibreChat: release tag, digest-verified against the build we deployed.
LIBRECHAT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat:v0.8.7
# LiteLLM's stable channel is a moving tag, so pin its digest (= LiteLLM 1.91.1):
LITELLM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:main-stable@sha256:47afa74b495c802317712e5b8c8a65e7ca30c96636e9b618a5f8130eec72a8ee
# The RAG API only publishes a dev channel — pin the digest we tested:
RAG_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat-rag-api-dev:latest@sha256:c3e1a05bdd576b5000fa0e8a84a476e9858fa9219b2b5d78432ddce12c9fcf23
# LibreChat admin panel publishes only a moving tag — pin the digest we tested:
ADMIN_PANEL_IMAGE=registry.librechat.ai/clickhouse/librechat-admin-panel:latest@sha256:9a78851f84f448eab780ac658c4d17db51974c240492affc789a72d61e35f678
# opencode coding harness (workbench profile): release tag, digest-verified
# (sha256:ef9257b3246e...) against the build we tested end-to-end:
OPENCODE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/anomalyco/opencode:1.18.2

# ---- Datastores.  Floating major tags were the pinning gap (2026-09-15):
# `mongo:7` moved whenever `just pull` felt like it.  Digest-pinned now.
# Moving one of THESE on stable is a data migration, not an image bump —
# Mongo wants a featureCompatibilityVersion step, Meili wants a dump.
MONGO_IMAGE=mongo:7@sha256:9854f7139445d766a9523571d6f047530c45547460ffcf8259eb2bf4264632ca
MEILI_IMAGE=getmeili/meilisearch:v1.12@sha256:c9fac23131cca4db95173d41cc50fd5639121ee381795528fdd7522d7978a7b8
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine@sha256:cf78e76683b9ca8c5733cbbdce6c9262b45b6767934dd0a95e671f9a0fc20685
PGVECTOR_IMAGE=pgvector/pgvector:pg16@sha256:ccc6e83d6e35e931dc7c5def2022729d5a6c370318d099181995567ff1fb4d6b
